6 Phases mein project divide kiya gaya hai:

Phase	         Kaam
Phase 1	         AWS environment setup + Boto3 se Bedrock test karna
Phase 2	         FastAPI backend banana (/chat endpoint)
Phase 3	         Python ko Bedrock se connect karna (Converse API)
Phase 4	         React frontend banana (chat UI)
Phase 5	         Frontend aur Backend ko integrate karna
Phase 6	         Improvements — history, streaming, model selection, usage tracking
___________________________________________________________________________________________________

Overall architecture

User (Browser)
      |
      | Types a message & clicks Send
      ↓
React.js Frontend  (runs on localhost:3000)
      |
      | HTTP POST /chat  →  JSON { "message": "..." }
      ↓
Python FastAPI Backend  (runs on localhost:8000)
      |
      | Boto3 SDK call
      ↓
Amazon Bedrock  (AWS Cloud - us-east-1)
      |
      | Foundation Model (Claude / Nova / Llama)
      ↓
AI Response returns back
      |
      ↓
FastAPI → React → User screen pe display


2. Step-by-Step Development Plan
✅ Phase 1 — AWS Environment Prepare Karo
AWS account mein Bedrock model access enable karo
IAM user/role ko sahi permissions do
Boto3 install karo aur ek simple Python script se Bedrock test karo
Milestone: Terminal mein Bedrock ka response print ho jaye
✅ Phase 2 — Python FastAPI Backend Banao
FastAPI project setup karo
Do endpoints banao:
GET / → Backend health check
POST /chat → User ka message lo, Bedrock se response lao
Milestone: Postman ya browser se /chat call karo aur response aaye
✅ Phase 3 — Backend ko Bedrock se Connect Karo
Boto3 se bedrock-runtime client banao
Converse API use karo prompt bhejne ke liye
Error handling lagao (wrong credentials, access denied, throttling)
Milestone: FastAPI ke through Bedrock ka real AI response aaye
✅ Phase 4 — React Frontend Banao
React project create karo
Yeh components banao:
Chat message area
User aur AI message bubbles
Text input box
Send button
Loading indicator
Pehle dummy responses se UI test karo
Milestone: Chatbot UI browser mein dikh rahi ho
✅ Phase 5 — Frontend aur Backend Integrate Karo
React se FastAPI ko HTTP request bhejo
Full flow test karo: React → FastAPI → Bedrock → FastAPI → React
Error handling add karo
Milestone: Browser mein real AI responses aa rahe hon
✅ Phase 6 — Improvements Karo
Conversation history (purani baatein yaad rahen)
Streaming responses (ChatGPT jaisa word-by-word aana)
Multiple chat sessions
Model selection (Claude, Nova, Llama choose kar sako)
Usage tracking (tokens aur invocations)

# project structure :-

bedrock-chatbot/
│
├── frontend/                        ← React Application
│   ├── public/
│   │   └── index.html
│   ├── src/
│   │   ├── components/
│   │   │   ├── ChatWindow.jsx       ← Messages display area
│   │   │   ├── Message.jsx          ← Single message bubble
│   │   │   └── ChatInput.jsx        ← Input box + Send button
│   │   ├── App.jsx                  ← Main app component
│   │   ├── App.css                  ← Styling
│   │   └── index.js                 ← React entry point
│   └── package.json                 ← Frontend dependencies
│
├── backend/                         ← Python FastAPI Application
│   ├── main.py                      ← FastAPI routes & app entry
│   ├── bedrock_service.py           ← Boto3 + Bedrock logic
│   ├── config.py                    ← Region, model ID, settings
│   └── requirements.txt             ← Python dependencies
│
├── .gitignore                       ← node_modules, __pycache__, .env ignore
└── README.md                        ← Setup instructions


4. AWS Prerequisites aur IAM Permissions
    AWS Account mein kya hona chahiye:
    Requirement	Kya karna hai
    AWS Account	Active hona chahiye
    Bedrock Model Access	AWS Console → Bedrock → Model Access → Enable karo
    AWS Region	us-east-1 recommend hai (tumhara existing setup bhi same hai)
    IAM User ya Role	Bedrock invoke karne ki permission ke saath
    Boto3	pip install boto3
    AWS Credentials	~/.aws/credentials mein configure karo


Step 1 — User message type karta hai
         React ka ChatInput.jsx → Send button click

Step 2 — React HTTP request bhejta hai
         POST http://localhost:8000/chat
         Body: { "message": "Explain Docker" }

Step 3 — FastAPI request receive karta hai
         main.py ka /chat endpoint trigger hota hai
         Input validate hota hai

Step 4 — FastAPI Bedrock ko call karta hai
         bedrock_service.py → Boto3 → Converse API
         Model: Claude ya Nova

Step 5 — Bedrock AI response generate karta hai
         Token usage, response text wapas aata hai

Step 6 — FastAPI response React ko bhejta hai
         JSON: { "response": "Docker ek platform hai..." }

Step 7 — React screen pe display karta hai
         ChatWindow.jsx mein AI message bubble add hota hai
